   "source": {
    "label": "th:lowerbound",
    "number": "Theorem 5",
    "quote": "Suppose $G_t = G$ for all $t$ with $\\alpha(G)>1$. There exist two constants $C_1,C_2 > 0$ such that whenever $T \\ge C_1\\alpha(G)^3$, then for any algorithm there exists an adversarial strategy for which the expected regret of the algorithm is at least $C_2\\sqrt{\\alpha(G) T}$."
   },
